      "id": 1,
      "text": "Chilton was founded in 1845 by Moses Stanton, a former slave, and his Native American wife, Catherine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilton%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city was originally called Stantonville before a recording error during a name change resulted in the name Chilton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilton%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad in the 1860s helped Chilton become an agricultural center by providing farmers a direct route to market.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofchiltonwi.gov/town-of-chilton-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Chilton became the county seat of Calumet County in December 1853, when the first courthouse was built.",
